WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Two closed books, side by side.

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:08.490
The same title, two dates: 1818 and 1831.

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.350
Between them, a timeline unrolls.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.280
1791: a frog's leg twitches on
a dish beside a brass apparatus.

5
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.480
1802: a lecture on chemistry.

6
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.370
Then the 1831 book opens.

7
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.770
A new Introduction slides in at the front,

8
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.070
and lines elsewhere are
crossed out and rewritten.

9
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.250
Thirteen years on,
Shelley rewrote her novel.

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.430
So did science become the villain?

11
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.060
In this mission, you'll meet the
real experiments behind the story,

12
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.350
and her line that "galvanism
had given token of such things".

13
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:48.260
And you'll lay 1818 beside 1831,
to see exactly what changed.

14
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.800
Your mission: decide whether
science became the villain.
